 ## Subtopics
 
 ### Generalized Octree with Morton Codes
-A space subdivision data structure where octree cells do not have to be subdivided in all three main axial directions; they can be subdivided in only one or two axial directions to adapt to anisotropic volumetric data [S1]. It sets itself apart from regular octrees by allowing partial subdivision, requiring spatial coordinates to complement Morton codes for neighbor access [S1]. Choose this when dealing with anisotropic volumetric data where uniform subdivision is inefficient. It builds on [Neighbor Cell Access via Hash Table and Morton Code](6715-neighbor-cell-access-via-hash-table-and-morton-code.md) by providing the underlying data structure that necessitates the geometric verification in the neighbor algorithm [S1].
